From 5b87d46eefdcbb276f1e15dd199deb6ea6b12893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 22:03:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 87/87] video: rockchip: fix defects found reviewing the
 previous five commits

Adversarial review of the audit fixes found that three of them were
wrong or incomplete. Corrections, in severity order:

RGA import_cnt counted every de-dup import, but session teardown spends
the count on the owner's behalf. Lookup is global, so a second session
de-dupping onto a buffer inflated the owner's count and its close then
handed back references it never held -- freeing the buffer under the
other session's handle, or under its running job. Count only the owner's
imports. This was a use-after-free introduced by the previous commit.

put_task_msgs() dropped the msgs fd reference before writing msgs->ext_fd,
resetting the object and taking session->lock_msgs. A sibling thread
closing that fd runs __fput() -- and mpp_session_deinit(), which kfree()s
every msgs and the session -- synchronously, so those three steps could
land in freed memory. Pre-existing, but the previous commit added two
call sites on exactly the fd-carrying object, including the first one
ever to put a freshly switched msgs. Drop the reference last.

Rejecting a bad session fd before the message flush kept the previous
msgs and appended the rest of the batch to it, merging two sub-batches
into one task: past MPP_MAX_MSG_NUM that discarded requests already
collected, and it bled the first sub-batch's msg_flags into the second's
register translation. Abort the batch instead.

Also: look up, check and put under one hold of list_mutex in
mpp_dma_release_fd(), since the split let a released slot be recycled
between the lookup and the check; keep releasing the rest of the
MPP_CMD_RELEASE_FD array after a failure and report the first error;
ratelimit its user-triggerable dev_err(); clear msgs->poll_req on reset,
now that error paths recycle the object; sync-cancel the timeout work in
the hard-CCU dequeue and resend paths too, which have the same shape as
the soft-CCU one already fixed; read and publish rkvdec2 cur_task under
running_lock in the fault handler and the enqueue, so the clear added
last commit actually excludes the reader; and let an fd import and a PTR
import of one dma_buf de-dup onto each other again, so MPI does not
re-attach and re-map per frame.

Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
